 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252866 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252866 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252866 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252866 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186251023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252866 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "225256aa-a878-5dbd-ac6b-c6508ad4090e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252781 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252956 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252956 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252956 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186251435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252956 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "569731a1-44d9-5454-8f2b-b1754aaefd2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186250663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186250816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253241 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253241 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253241 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186251947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253241 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f6690fcb-b915-5e44-8c44-d66de9e23524" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253561 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186253241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253561 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119290" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253561 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253561 #edb/ref 1071 "A population of $50\\,000\\,000$ people is being vaccinated against a disease. The rate of growth in the number of people $P(t)$ vaccinated is jointly proportional to the number of people who have been vaccinated at time $t,$ measured in months, and the number of unvaccinated people. If the constant of proportionality is $0.3,$ which differential equation could be used to model $P(t)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253561 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "69d6c7c8-a17d-5595-94e0-1820b1ec12de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253561 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the growth rate of vaccinated people is *jointly* proportional to the number of people who have been vaccinated at time $t,$ and the number of unvaccinated people, the number of vaccinated people follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.3,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=50\\,000\\,000.$ Therefore, the number of people who have been vaccinated is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.3P(50\\,000\\,000-P).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317591 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317591 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317591 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "06774482-8185-522a-b0da-abe466cad0be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318032 #edb/ref 1080 "188" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318032 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318032 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8ae082c6-947e-5375-a9f4-aa88253e382d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318510 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186318032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318510 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318510 #edb/ref 10